music BGM01.mp3
sound R7A.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text Up until six years ago, Koumura-sensei had been teaching at an industrial high school.
text Ibuki-san leans against the iron bar and starts talking.
sound R7B.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text For a time, the behaviour of the students there had become a problem, and the school had become famous for it.
text I knew the school she was talking about. It was an infamous school, containing all the town's delinquents.
sound R7C.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text And for a long time, he'd been working as a counselor there.
text @[Tomoya]
text With that frail body of his?
sound R7D.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text Of course he was far younger than he is now... Besides, that kind of thing doesn't take physical strength.
text @[Tomoya]
text Guess so...
sound R7E.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text At any rate, he was really strict.
text @[Tomoya]
text Seriously...?
sound R7F.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text Yes, it's really true. Sometimes he'd even throw the parents into the counseling room and give them a scolding too...
text I can't believe it...
sound R7G.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text He was pretty unconventional as a life coach...
sound R7H.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text But there was one principle he would never let go of.
text @[Tomoya]
text What was that?
sound R7I.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text He would definitely not let any students quit school.
sound R7J.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text He wouldn't even let them drop out of their own volition.
sound R7K.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text Koumura-sensei considered the school like a microcosm of life.
sound R7L.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text The three years you spend at school aren't just for studying.
sound R7M.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text They're to get in contact with people, make friends, and work together...
sound R7N.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text There are successes and failures...
sound R7O.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text Joy and pain...
sound R7P.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text Everyone there is walking toward the goal they set for themselves when they enrolled: graduation.
sound R7Q.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text If he let them quit this path halfway, or let them stop in frustration...
sound R7R.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text They would be set back in life, as well.
sound R7S.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text They wouldn't be able to face the even bigger world to come.
sound R7T.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text That's why he wouldn't just scold the students, but he would also walk alongside them, encouraging them.
sound R7U.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text But ever since he came to this school...
sound R7V.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text There was no need for him to do so anymore. You understand why, right?
sound R7W.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text It's because the students here are all excellent.
sound R7X.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text What he surely must have considered his duty, something that he absolutely had to do as a teacher...
sound R7Y.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text I think he must have spent these six years having that contradicted because he wasn't needed at all.
sound R7Z.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text It's because everyone only ever thought of the three years they would spend in that school as merely another step in their lives...
sound R80.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text So what he considered himself to be his duty wasn't at all needed here.
sound R81.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text And for six years, he continued feeling that way.
sound R82.aac
text @[Ibuki]
text And now this spring, his teaching career is going to come to an end.
text Ibuki-san finishes her story, and pulls away from the iron rod.
text She then faces my way.
